Revision history for WWW-MetaForge

{{$NEXT}}

 - Item: expose the API's used_in list, the items this item is a component of
 - Declare LWP::Protocol::https as a prerequisite; the API is HTTPS-only, so
   without it a fresh install died with "LWP::Protocol::https not installed"
   on the first request
 - Align the ARC Raiders result classes with the current live API response
   format; this changes which attributes are available and may be
   incompatible for code reading result fields:
   - Item: item_type, value, stat_block
   - Arc: simplified fields
   - Quest: nested rewards, trader_name, xp
   - Trader: inventory item fields
 - Add the riven-tides and stella-montis maps
 - Add the CLI subcommands `map <map-id>` (GameMapData markers, --type filter)
   and `trader <name>` (single-trader inventory)
 - Realign the Quest and Arc CLI commands with the live API; output of fields
   the API never sent is dropped
 - Add Result::Arc attribute `loot` (the CLI requests includeLoot=true) and
   Result::Quest attribute `guide_url`; `guide_links` is dead upstream
 - Fix the CLI item lookup not sending includeComponents, which left the
   crafting, sold-by and recycle sections empty
 - Fix Result::Quest::from_hashref reading camelCase keys the API does not
   send
 - The pagination stops after 100 pages and dies with an error instead of
   returning an incomplete answer
 - An API error names the method and the path of the request
 - The README names the cache directory and the maps that the code uses
 - The prerequisites name the distributions they come from: Types::Standard,
   which the type constraints need, and HTTP::Message, which ships
   HTTP::Request and HTTP::Response, so a fresh install loads the library
   instead of failing on a missing module; t/cpanfile.t holds the list

0.002     2026-01-11 04:45:55Z

 - Convert POD documentation to @Author::GETTY inline style

0.001     2026-01-05 05:03:59Z

 - Initial release
 - ARC Raiders API client (items, quests, traders, arcs, events, map data)
 - CLI tool: metaforge-arcraiders
 - Response caching with configurable TTL
